    multinomial-equivalence-4d9a3337.rds carries summaries - but
    bcf-equivalence-6e3b9fb8.rds still predates them, so a cross-host
    x86 CI run on THAT gate degrades loudly rather than passing
    statistically until it is re-recorded (a re-record is only valid
    from the recording host); AND a re-record alone is
    not sufficient: the non-statChannels entries (mu, tau, glue,
    varcount, varcount.tau; forestFits, varcount, accepted,
    installed) are live-sampler final-state snapshots that mismatch
    bitwise across hosts by construction, so a cross-host pass needs
    a further design decision - exempt snapshot channels under an
    explicit cross-host flag, or convert them to draws-axis
    recordings at a re-record - neither taken here. CI legs stay
    default-branch-gated regardless.
